      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The authors used a new method of treatment of prostatic cancer--selective stereotactic puncture cryodestruction of the anteriod hypophysis lobe--which prevents water-electrolyte imbalance, relieves pain syndrome due to bone metastases, reduces androgenic stimulation of the prostate, improves quality of life for patients of clinical group IV. The operation is low-traumatic and is not accompanied with serious complications."},
